      <activity id="54da463f-3210-5a19-8671-e22766c3a93b" activityNameId="03688ad0-7f55-5193-a69d-fb67f00ec5bd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by conversion of methanol using fuel cell, DMFC allocated by exergy, distributed by truc [657fff86d5]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by conversion of methanol using fuel cell, DMFC allocated by exergy, distributed by truck, produced by Electrolysis, PEM using electricity from grid and carbon sourced from Cement plant (100:0 alloc.)
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by methanol conversion in a fuel cell, DMFC.  The methanol is distributed by truck from regional storage.  The methanol is produced from hydrogen supplied by  Electrolysis, PEM, with electricity from grid as feedstock. The carbon is sourced from Cement plant. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 50%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 20. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Distribution loss [% output]: 0%. Storage loss [% output]: 0%. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Hydrogen production efficiency [% LHV input]: 0. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 3.33. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 5.88%. Power [kW]: 1.67. Lifetime [years]: 2.93. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. : .  For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: e303a616-c3fe-3941-ab7d-8149ce89336e
